§ `s 9 -- may a corporation sue` -- d062: Jarrah

#ASSERT NOT `Is my company an excluded corporation` `Jarrah in 2040`
#ASSERT `Is my company an excluded corporation` `Jarrah in its first year, three staff`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my company an excluded corporation` `a small subsidiary of a group`
#ASSERT `Is my company an excluded corporation` `a charity with 200 staff`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my company an excluded corporation` `eight full-timers and four half-timers`

§ `ss 7-10, 23 -- may I sue` -- d062: Jarrah cannot; Daniel can over what the post says of him

#ASSERT `May I sue for defamation` `the false post, Jarrah suing` EQUALS `no: a corporation that was not an excluded corporation at the time of publication (s 9(1))`
#ASSERT `May I sue for defamation` `the false post, Daniel suing over what it says of him` EQUALS `yes: a cause of action for defamation, without proof of special damage (ss 7, 8)`
#ASSERT `May I sue for defamation` `a post about Daniel's late father` EQUALS `no: no cause of action about a deceased person (s 10(a))`
#ASSERT `May I sue for defamation` `a post by someone who has since died` EQUALS `no: no cause of action against a publisher who has died since publishing (s 10(b))`
#ASSERT `May I sue for defamation` `a second action over the same post, without leave` EQUALS `yes, but only with the leave of the court, having sued this publisher over this matter before (s 23)`
#ASSERT `May I sue for defamation` `a post that carries no defamatory imputation` EQUALS `no: the matter carries no defamatory imputation (general law)`

§ `Limitation Act 2005 ss 15, 40 -- by when` -- d062: published 30 June 2040

#ASSERT `Am I in time to sue` 11 FALSE EQUALS `in time: less than one year since publication (Limitation Act s 15)`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to sue` 12 FALSE EQUALS `out of time unless the court extends it, which it must if satisfied it was not reasonable to sue within the year (Limitation Act s 40(2))`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to sue` 35 TRUE EQUALS `in time only because the court has extended it (Limitation Act s 40(2))`
#ASSERT `Am I in time to sue` 36 TRUE EQUALS `too late: 3 years have elapsed since publication (Limitation Act s 40(3))`

§ `s 14 -- the concerns notice` -- d062: Daniel's notice

#ASSERT `Is my notice a concerns notice` `Daniel's concerns notice`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my notice a concerns notice` `a phone call to the poster`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my notice a concerns notice` `a letter naming no imputations`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my notice a concerns notice` `particulars given 20 days after a request`
#ASSERT `Is my notice a concerns notice` `particulars given 20 days after a request, 7 more days agreed`

#ASSERT `What does my notice do` `Daniel's concerns notice` EQUALS `it starts the publisher's 28 days to make an offer to make amends (s 14(1)(a)); this edition does not require it before I sue`
#ASSERT `What does my notice do` `a phone call to the poster` EQUALS `nothing under the Act: it is not a concerns notice (s 14(2), (5)); this edition does not require one before I sue`

§ `ss 14(1), 16(5) -- was the offer in time` -- d062

#ASSERT `Was the offer to make amends made in time` `Daniel's offer, 10 days after his notice`
#ASSERT NOT `Was the offer to make amends made in time` `an offer 28 days after the notice`
#ASSERT NOT `Was the offer to make amends made in time` `an offer after a defence was served`
#ASSERT `Was the offer to make amends made in time` `a genuine renewed offer 40 days after the notice, 10 days after withdrawal`
#ASSERT NOT `Was the offer to make amends made in time` `a genuine renewed offer 40 days after the notice, 20 days after withdrawal`

§ `s 15 -- what the offer must contain` -- d062

#ASSERT `Does the offer meet the requirements of s 15` `the offer to Daniel`
#ASSERT NOT `Does the offer meet the requirements of s 15` `an offer with no correction`
#ASSERT NOT `Does the offer meet the requirements of s 15` `a limited offer that does not say so`

§ `ss 17, 18 -- accepting or refusing` -- d062: the offer accepted

#ASSERT `What happens if I accept the offer` `Daniel's offer, 10 days after his notice` `the offer to Daniel` TRUE EQUALS `I can no longer sue this publisher over the matter: the accepted offer has been carried out (s 17(1))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I accept the offer` `Daniel's offer, 10 days after his notice` `the offer to Daniel` FALSE EQUALS `not yet barred: the publisher has not carried out the accepted offer; a court may decide what must be done (s 15(3))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I accept the offer` `an offer 28 days after the notice` `the offer to Daniel` TRUE EQUALS `no effect under the Act: it is not an offer to make amends (ss 14, 15)`

#ASSERT `Does my refusal give the publisher a defence` `Daniel's offer, 10 days after his notice` `the offer to Daniel` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my refusal give the publisher a defence` `Daniel's offer, 10 days after his notice` `the offer to Daniel` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `ss 25, 26, 31, 33 -- the publisher's defences` -- d062: a false post

#ASSERT `Which defence defeats my claim` `a false statement of fact` EQUALS `none of these defences`
#ASSERT `Which defence defeats my claim` `a true statement` EQUALS `justification: the imputations are substantially true (s 25)`
#ASSERT `Which defence defeats my claim` `a stinging but true context` EQUALS `contextual truth (s 26)`
#ASSERT `Which defence defeats my claim` `an honest opinion on proper material` EQUALS `honest opinion (s 31(1))`
#ASSERT `Which defence defeats my claim` `an opinion the poster did not hold` EQUALS `none of these defences`

§ `ss 35, 37 -- damages`

#ASSERT `What will the next maximum damages amount be` 250000 3.5 EQUALS 259000
#ASSERT `What will the next maximum damages amount be` 300000 3.1 EQUALS 309500

#ASSERT `How much can I get for non-economic loss` `a large award, no aggravation` 250000 EQUALS 250000
#ASSERT `How much can I get for non-economic loss` `a large award, aggravated` 250000 EQUALS 400000

#ASSERT `How much can I be awarded in all` `a large award, no aggravation` 250000 EQUALS 300000

